   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.5. Increased capacity of member States to formulate and implement labour market programmes and employment services for transitions to decent work over the life course, with particular focus on young and older workers</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In February 2021, the Ministry of Labour approved the an assessment of the Public Employment Services (PES) and its accompanying roadmap for strengthening service delivery. As a first step, the capacity of key PES staff has been strengthened based on international practice.
 In 2020, the ILO completed a PES assessment and developed recommendations for the operationalization of the PES component of the National Employment Strategy. The report was presented at a validation workshop in February 2021. As a follow up to the Social Dialogue Conference in March, the ILO and the Ministry of Labour discussed the main priority interventions for improving PES particularly during times of emergency.

The ILO sponsored the participation of staff of the PES in a training course organized by the Turin Centre.</narrative>
   </description>
