  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.1. Increased capacity of member States to formulate and implement a new generation of gender-responsive national employment policies, including for youth</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In November 2020, the Palestinian Cabinet adopted its first National Employment Strategy (NES), covering the period 2021-2025. The NES was launched during a Social Dialogue Conference in March 2021 and includes youth and women as main target groups. With support from the Government of Kuwait, the ILO provided technical and financial support to the NES development process. An employment diagnostic was first initiated by the ILO in 2018, using a participatory approach involving the Ministry of Labour (MOL), trade unions, and employers&apos; organisations, and based on which a policy paper with 3 priority areas was developed with a recommendation to establish a tripartite inter-ministerial committee to elaborate on the policy interventions under the three priority areas. 
The ILO provided technical support to this inter-ministerial committee and facilitated its meetings and consultations, to ensure an inclusive policy formulation process.

The ILO delivered in 2019 a capacity building and training workshop on inclusive employment policy development and action plan formulation, aiming also to sensitize tripartite stakeholders to relevant international labour standards and ILO conventions.
With the spread of COVID-19, the ILO conducted a study on the labour market impact of the crisis, finalized in September 2020, providing further analysis and feeding into the development of a NES, that also takes into account the impact of the crisis.

The drafting of the policy was led by the ILO supported by a team of senior consultants and in consultation with national tripartite stakeholders.</narrative>
   </description>
